WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.915
Roscoe and the others shook with fear.

2
00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:08.237
Finally he took a deep breath.

3
00:00:08.238 --> 00:00:11.133
"I'm the sheriff," Roscoe thought.

4
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:13.660
"I have to be brave."

5
00:00:13.661 --> 00:00:18.699
He turned to the others. "Follow me!"

6
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.561
They all ran fast.

7
00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:25.933
As they turned a corner, the ghosts appeared in front of them.

8
00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.637
Roscoe and his friends spun around.

9
00:00:28.638 --> 00:00:32.005
But the ghosts appeared before them again.

10
00:00:32.006 --> 00:00:35.292
"What do you want?" Roscoe yelled.

11
00:00:35.293 --> 00:00:38.307
The little girl held out her arm.

12
00:00:38.308 --> 00:00:41.941
The blank canvas jumped from Annie's paws.

13
00:00:41.942 --> 00:00:44.599
"Hey!" Annie said.

14
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.465
The canvas floated to the ghosts.

15
00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:54.042
The word "stay" appeared on it.

16
00:00:54.043 --> 00:00:58.227
Roscoe gasped. "She's trying to talk to us!"

17
00:00:58.228 --> 00:01:00.948
Cleo laughed nervously.

18
00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:07.665
"Um, thanks for the invitation. But we have to leave."

19
00:01:07.666 --> 00:01:11.978
Now the word "lonely" appeared.

20
00:01:11.979 --> 00:01:16.464
"You're lonely?" Cleo asked.

21
00:01:16.465 --> 00:01:20.377
The three ghosts nodded.

22
00:01:20.378 --> 00:01:23.334
"Hmph!" Roscoe folded his arms.

23
00:01:23.335 --> 00:01:26.446
"They have a strange way of making us feel welcome."

24
00:01:26.447 --> 00:01:29.988
"That's for sure," Annie whispered.

25
00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:35.251
Just then her half-finished painting floated to the ghosts.

26
00:01:35.252 --> 00:01:40.919
The word "pretty" appeared on the blank canvas.

27
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:46.985
"Annie," Cleo said. "I think they like your painting."

28
00:01:46.986 --> 00:01:51.813
Annie was still shaking. "They can have it!"

29
00:01:51.814 --> 00:01:54.620
Roscoe stepped forward.

30
00:01:54.621 --> 00:01:57.849
"We'll give you the painting if you let us go."

31
00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.699
The ghosts didn't move.

32
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:06.840
"What do you want from us?" Roscoe asked.

33
00:02:06.841 --> 00:02:10.360
"More."

34
00:02:10.361 --> 00:02:14.638
Suddenly Roscoe understood.

35
00:02:14.639 --> 00:02:24.231
"Miss Annie, you'd better start painting."

36
00:02:24.232 --> 00:02:29.059
Inside the saloon Roscoe hung up a new painting.

37
00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.625
It showed the saloon.

38
00:02:31.626 --> 00:02:35.873
But in the painting, the place was brand-new.

39
00:02:35.874 --> 00:02:40.981
Roscoe, Cleo, and Annie sat at a table.

40
00:02:40.982 --> 00:02:46.898
The man with the bowtie played the piano as the girl danced.

41
00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:51.410
The outlaw sat at the bar, looking happy.

42
00:02:51.411 --> 00:02:58.519
The ghosts went closer to the painting and stared at it, smiling.

43
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:03.273
Roscoe went over to Cleo and Annie. "Let's get out of here."

44
00:03:03.274 --> 00:03:10.378
They tiptoed to the door and slipped outside.

45
00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:23.756
They ran to their horses, jumped on, and took off!

46
00:03:23.757 --> 00:03:28.217
"I can't believe we saw real ghosts!" Cleo said.

47
00:03:28.218 --> 00:03:31.785
"I'm glad they liked my new painting," Annie said.

48
00:03:31.786 --> 00:03:34.506
"Maybe they won't be lonely now."

49
00:03:34.507 --> 00:03:37.992
"Ahem." Roscoe cleared his throat.

50
00:03:37.993 --> 00:03:42.404
He wanted to tell Annie how much he liked her painting.

51
00:03:42.405 --> 00:03:46.034
"I . . . uh . . ."

52
00:03:46.035 --> 00:03:51.518
Aw, shucks! That tough old dog didn't know what to say!

53
00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:56.036
Luckily it was Annie's turn to come to the rescue.

54
00:03:56.037 --> 00:04:00.424
"It gets lonely out here in the West," she said.

55
00:04:00.425 --> 00:04:05.062
"It's nice to have newcomers in town."

56
00:04:05.063 --> 00:04:10.835
The sheriff's face turned red. "It's nice to be here."

57
00:04:10.836 --> 00:04:20.922
His deputy rolled her eyes.

